# The backend API's base URL — read by browser-side code (NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix), so it must be set before the Next.js dev server starts;
# restart the frontend container after changing it, a hot-reload alone
# won't pick it up.
#
# Left unset by default. When unset, lib/utils/api.ts derives the
# backend's address at runtime from whatever host/IP the browser used
# to load the frontend itself (same machine, port 3012) — this is what
# keeps external-device access working automatically as this host's
# public/LAN IP changes across networks, with nothing to edit.
#
# Only set this if the backend runs on a genuinely different host or
# port than the frontend.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3012
